  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/sep100-700.html",
  "prefLabel": "Sep 401.02 Renewal of License",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Sep 401.02 Renewal of License.\n\n(a) Any licensee wishing to renew a license shall submit:\n\n(1) A completed “Universal Application for License Renewal”, as described in Plc 308.05, in which the applicant provides the information required in Plc 308.06, the documentation described in Plc 308.07, and signs the form pursuant to Plc 308.08;\n\n(2) The fee specified in Plc 1002.49;\n\n(3) Proof of completion of the continuing education requirements of Sep 403; and\n\n(4) If applicable, a copy of the licensee’s military orders calling them to active duty pursuant to Sep 401.02 (b).\n\n(b) Licensees who are serving in the armed forces or the reserves or the national guard of the United States that is called to active duty, may submit a completed “Request for Inactive Status – Military Activation” form dated March 2024 and provide the information required by Plc 307.06 to the licensing bureau. Licensees may submit a “Request for License Reactivation” form to provide the information specified in Plc 307.07, within one year of the licensee’s release from active status, to reactivate their license.\n\nSource. #12654, eff 10-31-18; ss by #14361, eff 10-26-25, EXPIRES: 10-26-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/sep100-700.html"
}
